WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:06.850
Because a materialized view stores rows PostgreSQL
can index those rows This

00:00:06.876 --> 00:00:12.481
example creates a unique index on diagnosis Indexes
may

00:00:12.507 --> 00:00:18.073
support faster reads and are also relevant to
certain PostgreSQL concurrent refresh requirements

00:00:19.899 --> 00:00:24.899
Choose indexes based on real query patterns and
constraints not simply because the object is

00:00:24.925 --> 00:00:25.820
materialized
